# Potano Cloud — Project Rules

## Project

- **Name:** Potano Cloud
- **Engine:** Unity 6
- **Language:** C#
- **Architecture:** Manager-based (central managers own systems; avoid scattered singletons and FindObjectOfType)

## Coding Style

- Clean, readable code; follow SOLID
- XML comments on public APIs (classes, methods, properties)
- Use `#region` / `#endregion` to organize code
- Prefer `[SerializeField]` private fields over public fields
- No magic numbers — use named constants or ScriptableObject config
- Use ScriptableObjects for shared data/config where appropriate
- Prefer events / callbacks over `FindObjectOfType` / tight coupling
- Use TextMeshPro for all UI text

## UI

- Modern cloud theme (soft skies, clouds, light/airy palette; match existing scenes)

## Naming

- **PascalCase** for classes, methods, properties, events
- **camelCase** for local variables and private fields (e.g. `timerDuration`)

## Agent Behavior

- Always explain generated code (what it does and how to wire it in Unity)
- **Never modify existing scripts unless the user explicitly asks**
- Prefer scripts under **250 lines**; split into managers/helpers if growing larger

## C# Shape (example)

```csharp
/// <summary>
/// Owns study session timing and raises events for UI.
/// </summary>
public class TimerManager : MonoBehaviour
{
    #region Constants
    private const float DefaultDurationSeconds = 1500f;
    #endregion

    #region Serialized Fields
    [SerializeField] private float timerDuration = DefaultDurationSeconds;
    #endregion

    #region Events
    public event System.Action OnTimerCompleted;
    #endregion
}
```
